  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/machine/fields.rs`: the \"Spindle range\" group gave each of its three fields the refusal key `spindle`. That key holds one refusal only: `min_speed` above `max_speed` (`crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs`). Now only Spindle min speed and Spindle max speed carry `spindle`. Spindle power keeps its own key `spindle power`.\n- The machine editor (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/machine_file_editor.rs`) reads `Field::refusals` for each field. Thus the UI needs no change.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe reporter's steps, through `MachineDraft`: a blank mill, Spindle min speed 1000, Spindle max speed 24.\n\n| Field | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Spindle min speed | `spindle: min_speed 1000 must not exceed max_speed 24` | the same |\n| Spindle max speed | `spindle: min_speed 1000 must not exceed max_speed 24` | the same |\n| Spindle power | `spindle: min_speed 1000 must not exceed max_speed 24` | no refusal |\n\nThe refusal still has a field: `fields::unplaced` stays empty.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `machine_field_refusals::the_spindle_speed_refusal_sits_on_the_speed_fields_and_not_on_spindle_power` (new file `crates/app/tests/machine_field_refusals.rs`). It asserts the table above. It also asserts that a power of -3 puts one `spindle power:` refusal on Spindle power.\n  - Without the fix, the test fails at the Spindle power assert with `[\"spindle: min_speed 1000 must not exceed max_speed 24\"]`.\n  - The test has its own file because `crates/app/tests/machine_edit.rs` has 406 lines (the 400-line rule).\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the head 638380ddc:\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 4 steps, 0 failed. It includes `app suites: lib`, `app suites: machine_edit` and `app suites: machine_field_refusals`.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-app -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`): 68 steps (67 app heavy and 1 build), 1 failed (47.2 min). The 4 known-fail steps are red as expected.\n  - The red step is `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm`, test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`. It fails at the mesh pin (`pocket3d_hsm.rs:80`): the STEP mesh has 5232 facets, and the pin is 6228. This PR does not touch the import or the mesh. #3886 reports this step red on `main`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No check by hand in the GUI. The editor shows `Field::refusals` for each field, and the test asserts that list.\n\nChangelog: The machine editor shows the spindle min/max speed refusal only under the two speed fields, not under Spindle power.\n\nBranch made from `upstream/main` at 97a676e5c.\n\nFixes #3246\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
